  body: "# Accommodation and a fixed address in JSA(IB) and IS\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\nFor the
    captured special-case guidance, accommodation is described through shelter, heating capability, domestic
    activities and suitability for continuous occupation; the absence of a fixed address is expressly
    distinguished from having no accommodation.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\nThis is a source-specific
    meaning, not a homelessness-law definition. DMG 24156 says its special applicable-amount rule does
    not affect JSA(Cont). The source distinguishes motor cars from suitably equipped mobile motor homes
    and includes temporary-absence qualifications; no real person’s housing or entitlement status is inferred.\n\
    \n## Inspected source passages\n\n- [DMG 24157, PDF page 33](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e9f006886650c031ce2c41b/dmgch24.pdf#page=33)
    — DMG Vol 4 Ch 24: Special cases.\n- [DMG 24158, PDF page 33](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e9f006886650c031ce2c41b/dmgch24.pdf#page=33)
    — DMG Vol 4 Ch 24: Special cases.\n- [DMG 24160, PDF page 34](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e9f006886650c031ce2c41b/dmgch24.pdf#page=34)
    — DMG Vol 4 Ch 24: Special cases.\n- [DMG 24161, PDF page 34](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e9f006886650c031ce2c41b/dmgch24.pdf#page=34)
    — DMG Vol 4 Ch 24: Special cases.\n\n## Evidence and review status\n\nModel-assisted interpretation
    of selected passages in the 15 September 2026 frozen source snapshot. Specialist review is required.
    Source acquisition, source revision, legal effective dates and this record’s authoring time are separate.\n\
    \nThis is an independent experimental publication, not an official DWP document, individual advice,
    an entitlement decision or an executable rule. Machine-extracted text may alter reading order, footnotes
    and characters. No PDF visual inspection, whole-chapter coverage or behavioural evaluation pass is
    claimed by this record.\n\n- `dmg-vol4-ch24`: PDF SHA-256 `2827c11c3ce95e852073142524e0410c6534f7bf140d885be18cad09f6ece98a`;
    extracted pages SHA-256 `91863ddf195bf30158383f17cb2653f1ba498551a695c8ec0ba1e138d00a222c`.\n"
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/jsais-applicable-amount
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The chapter connects its accommodation finding with a particular JSA(IB)/IS
      applicable-amount rule and expressly excludes JSA(Cont).
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol4-ch24/0033
      quote: "24156   Where a DM decides that a claimant has no accommodation the applicable amount\n\
        \        should include only the normal personal allowance for the claimant and any\n        partner1.
        The DM cannot for example include dependants allowances, housing\n        costs, premiums or TE.\n\
        \n        Note: JSA(Cont) is not affected by this guidance.\n                         1 JSA Regs,
        reg 85 & Sch 5, para 3 & Sch 5A, para 2; IS (Gen) Regs, reg 21 & Sch 7, para 6"
      locator: DMG 24156
    - page: page/dmg-vol4-ch24/0033
      quote: "24157   DMG 24156 applies only to people without accommodation. The fact that a person\n\
        \        may have no fixed address is not relevant to the decision.\n\n\n        Meaning of accommodation"
      locator: DMG 24157
